# The generated Go project `hive build`/`hive run` writes beside the
# entrypoint, and the native executable it leaves there.
main.hive-build/
main
main.exe

# The same folder for every other entrypoint the compiler is pointed at —
# each test file gets one of its own on every `hive test`.
*.hive-build/

# What a design review leaves behind: the screenshots it judged and the
# sketches a direction was chosen from. The design itself — DESIGN.md,
# .impeccable/design.json and the surface briefs — stays in the repository.
.impeccable/review/
.impeccable/mocks/

*.log

# What `hive agents` writes for a coding agent to read: one short page per
# feature of the language, out of the compiler that ran it. Regenerated rather
# than committed, so that it can never describe a compiler nobody here has.
.hivedocs/
